1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,963
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:15,181
<i>Due to insufficient testimonies</i>
<i>and evidence submitted in court,</i>

3
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:18,727
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo and Raul Torillo</i>

4
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:21,646
<i>are hereby declared innocent of the rape,</i>

5
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:26,359
<i>abduction, and illegal</i>
<i>imprisonment of Camia Cruz.</i>

6
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:31,656
<i>We all know why the case against</i>
<i>the Ardientes was dismissed.</i>

7
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,826
<i>Because they threatened</i>
<i>and had the witnesses killed</i>

8
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:38,538
<i>so no one could prove</i>
<i>the crimes they committed.</i>

9
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:42,000
[Emilia] <i>I'll silence Camia once</i>
<i>and for all to solve our problem.</i>

10
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:44,294
<i>Slow down, Emilia. Camia Cruz?</i>

11
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,963
<i>She's too high a risk to take right now.</i>

12
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:49,591
[Julio] <i>What are you doing in my office?</i>

13
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:53,303
<i>I want you to keep an eye on Madrigal.</i>

14
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>Even if you have me killed now,</i>
<i>your husband will never love you!</i>

15
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:58,683
<i>Oh, well, you want more?!</i>

16
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,894
<i>Emilia, that's enough!</i>

17
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:04,105
<i>I can't stop myself from protecting you</i>

18
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,108
<i>when they're hurting you</i>
<i>right in front of me!</i>

19
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,152
<i>She did it to protect Camia.</i>

20
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:11,404
<i>I need to find out how they're connected.</i>

21
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:15,492
[Julio] <i>I can smell traitors</i>
<i>from a mile away.</i>

22
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:19,746
<i>Good work, Arnaldo.</i>
<i>We finally caught the rat.</i>

23
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>Take him to the dungeon.</i>

24
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:24,626
<i>You bastard! I trusted you!</i>

25
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,544
<i>And this is how you repay me?!</i>

26
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,630
[Ivy] <i>I need to save Jepoy.</i>

27
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:30,548
<i>Is that how important Jepoy is to you?</i>

28
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:33,051
<i>Yes, Diego. He's done so much for me.</i>

29
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,887
<i>He's sacrificed a lot</i>
<i>just so I can carry out my plans.</i>

30
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:38,389
<i>Ivy's here. Can I bring her there?</i>

31
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:39,557
<i>Why? What are you up to?</i>

32
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:43,645
[ominous music playing]

33
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:51,820
Uh… If Emilia looks for me,

34
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:54,197
please tell her I'm in the ladies' room.

35
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,448
Yes, ma'am.

36
00:01:56,658 --> 00:02:00,662
[ominous music playing]

37
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:03,182
[action music playing]

38
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:30,084
[tense music playing]

39
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:50,146
[door opens]

40
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,197
Fabian. Where's Ivy?

41
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:00,573
She's in the restroom, ma'am.

42
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:01,658
Oh.

43
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:14,963
[action music playing]

44
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:26,432
Ivy?

45
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:31,437
[action music playing]

46
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,107
Ivy, are you there?

47
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,152
Ivy?

48
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:45,201
[action music playing]

49
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:50,123
Ivy?

50
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:52,750
Is everything okay?

51
00:04:57,755 --> 00:04:59,382
Fabian, get the keys.

52
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:04,929
Fabian!

53
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,848
Hurry up, will you?!

54
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,141
Sorry, ma'am.

55
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:09,559
Give me that!

56
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,145
Goodness! Why didn't you label your keys?

57
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,147
See which one opens the door! Hurry!

58
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:18,401
You're supposed to label them!

59
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:19,777
Good grief!

60
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:25,658
[Emilia] Goodness… Hurry up!

61
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:26,909
Never mind!

62
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,995
Give me that! Get out of my sight!

63
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:33,416
[action music playing]

64
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:37,420
[door opening]

65
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,172
Ivy!

66
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,549
My goodness!

67
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:43,593
-Emilia?
-I've been calling you out!

68
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:44,927
Why weren't you answering?

69
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:49,265
Oh, sorry! I didn't hear you because…

70
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:52,310
you know…

71
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:54,937
You look tense. Why are you sweating?

72
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:57,690
Um…

73
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:03,488
Because it's summer, but there's
no AC in your restroom.

74
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:04,781
You should have one installed.

75
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:06,115
Well, okay.

76
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,992
Anyway, are you busy today?

77
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:11,579
Not really. Why?

78
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,749
Good. You're coming with me then.

79
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,293
Where are we going?

80
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,837
It's a surprise. You'll see.

81
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:21,756
Let's go.

82
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:25,760
[ominous music playing]

83
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:33,684
Emilia, what is this place?

84
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,104
This is Papa's happy place.

85
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,065
Your father's happy place?

86
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:41,651
What are we doing here, then?

87
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:43,111
You'll see.

88
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:46,155
[tense music playing]

89
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:50,159
[deep breathing]

90
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:55,873
I must admit, Madrigal.

91
00:06:58,376 --> 00:06:59,585
You really are tough.

92
00:07:08,302 --> 00:07:10,096
-Papa.
-Yes?

93
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:13,182
I have someone with me. Surprise!

94
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:15,935
Oh!

95
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:19,981
[tense music playing]

96
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,450
Miss Aguas.

97
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:40,793
I just want you to see what we do…

98
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,421
to anyone…

99
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,467
who betrays the Ardientes!

100
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,093
[Jepoy coughing]

101
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:57,518
[retches]

102
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,574
I'm sorry, but I don't think
I should be seeing this.

103
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,410
Emilia, why did you bring me here?

104
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,621
Not so fast, Ivy.

105
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,247
You see, it's not every day

106
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:21,000
Papa allows visitors like you here.

107
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:23,252
I brought you here because I trust you,

108
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,046
because I know we're allies.

109
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:28,758
Only a selected few are allowed
by Papa to come here.

110
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,843
And if you're one of those few,

111
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:33,763
that means you're bonded
with the Ardientes.

112
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:35,056
You know what, Ivy?

113
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:39,435
I'm actually giving you a great honor

114
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,772
because I'm offering you the chance

115
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:46,150
to be truly a part of my family.

116
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:49,654
But then again, before that happens…

117
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:53,032
you will have to prove your loyalty to us.

118
00:08:54,408 --> 00:08:55,952
Because if there's one thing I hate…

119
00:08:57,245 --> 00:09:00,498
it's backstabbing traitors!

120
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:04,544
[tense music playing]

121
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:16,472
Kill the man in front of you.

122
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:22,645
Kill Madrigal in front of us…

123
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,648
to prove that we're no different.

124
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:35,157
Kill Madrigal!

125
00:09:38,452 --> 00:09:40,079
Shoot the damn dog!

126
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,457
Do it.

127
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:51,966
[suspenseful music]

128
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:10,776
-[gunshot]
-[groans]

129
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:22,246
[Jepoy exhales sharply]

130
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:29,003
[chuckles]

131
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:30,212
Did I scare you?

132
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:31,505
[drops gun]

133
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:39,347
I won't taint my hands
just to prove my loyalty!

134
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:43,559
When I tell you to shoot him,
you will shoot him!

135
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,102
And that's an order!

136
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:47,480
Don't you dare tell me what to do, Emilia!

137
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:50,024
Because I'm not one of your
father's lackeys, unlike you!

138
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:51,150
Well, of course!

139
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:56,739
Not unless you're taking orders
from someone else, Miss Aguas.

140
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:59,325
Just what do you mean by that?

141
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:03,663
You know, my old man used to say…

142
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:06,832
if you truly want to know a person…

143
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:13,422
watch what they do and not what they say.

144
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:17,093
You distributed lands to the farmers…

145
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:23,307
defended Camia against my daughter Emilia…

146
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:27,436
and a host of other things
that you've done that left

147
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,813
a bad taste in my mouth.

148
00:11:29,438 --> 00:11:30,648
Now, Miss Aguas…

149
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:35,986
It seems like you're not
who you say you are.

150
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:42,701
[tense piano music playing]

151
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,455
Tell me, Congressman.

152
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:49,792
Why are you so paranoid?

153
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:51,752
[chuckles]

154
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:56,966
All my life, my family and I
have been bombarded

155
00:11:57,049 --> 00:12:01,595
on all sides by unseen enemies.

156
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:05,099
Now, please. Humor me, Miss Aguas.

157
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:09,437
Even just once, let me be able
to face my enemies…

158
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:14,358
and look at them straight in the eye.

159
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:20,823
You think I'm your enemy, Congressman?

160
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:28,038
You insult me. To the
highest degree, Congressman.

161
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:32,042
The next time you accuse
your biggest investor,

162
00:12:32,668 --> 00:12:38,174
I won't think twice before
siding with your greatest rival.

163
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:40,259
Once that happens,

164
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:43,471
that's the only time
you can call me a traitor!

165
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:49,185
But for now, my word is as good as gold!

166
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,437
Gold melts!

167
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:55,983
Even if it melts, it is still gold.

168
00:12:56,066 --> 00:12:59,653
[tense music playing]

169
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:16,128
[line ringing]

170
00:13:18,756 --> 00:13:19,757
Mrs. Camia.

171
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:21,133
Hey, Diego.

172
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:24,386
Any updates? Where's Lily?

173
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:27,097
Mrs. Camia, please calm down.

174
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:29,266
She hasn't been answering my calls.

175
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,269
Diego, be honest.

176
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:35,105
Does this have something to do
with Jepoy's disappearance?

177
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:37,691
[tense music playing]

178
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:39,735
Yes.

179
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:42,530
She's with the Ardientes,
looking for Jepoy.

180
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,031
What?

181
00:13:50,371 --> 00:13:52,206
<i>I'll save you, Jepoy.</i>

182
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:53,749
<i>I'll get you out of here.</i>

183
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,961
<i>I'll fight for you like how you fight me.</i>

184
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:58,629
I promise, Jepoy.

185
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,422
I'll save you.

186
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:09,723
After everything that
just transpired here…

187
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:13,644
I still don't trust that woman.

188
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:18,399
What if she tells everyone
we have Madrigal?

189
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:21,735
Our names will be caught
in another controversy.

190
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:24,071
What do you expect Emilia to do?

191
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:27,783
Lock Ivy Aguas up like Madrigal?

192
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:31,370
Should we lock up everyone you suspect?

193
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:34,665
-[loud thump]
-If that's what it takes

194
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:37,668
to keep this family afloat, yes!

195
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:41,755
Papa… none of us trust Ivy.

196
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:45,426
But unlike you, I know how
to sleep with the enemy.

197
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:49,138
I have to keep her close
to get information.

198
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:56,687
Arnaldo, keep an eye on Ivy Aguas.

199
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:59,231
I want you to watch her like a hawk.

200
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:02,651
Watch every move she makes.

201
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:08,782
Because, unlike your mother here
who thinks she's our ally,

202
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:13,746
treat her as if she's our greatest enemy.

203
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:17,666
I'm sorry, Emilia.

204
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:22,379
But your father
is just not the trusting type.

205
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:27,927
[action music playing]

206
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:33,265
I was right! Jepoy is with the Ardientes!

207
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,351
<i>They have him locked</i>
<i>and tied up somewhere.</i>

208
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:39,355
Emilia and Julio are
torturing him for information.

209
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:41,732
Ivy, you and Miss Camia need to leave.

210
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,817
It's too dangerous if Jepoy rats us out.

211
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:46,278
No. I know Jepoy. He won't betray us.

212
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,155
He'll stay loyal until his last breath.

213
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,074
<i>I'll break Jepoy out. I know…</i>

214
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,325
where they're keeping him.

215
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:52,576
I'll sneak in and get him.

216
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:54,286
How are you going to do that?

217
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:56,997
The Ardientes have their eyes on you.

218
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,958
I'll find a way!

219
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:03,504
[suspenseful music playing]

220
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:04,880
All right. Just follow that car.

221
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:11,261
<i>I'll finally know if you're</i>
<i>really connected to Camia Cruz.</i>

222
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:13,806
<i>But I hope you're not.</i>

223
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:16,100
<i>I hope you're not.</i>

224
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:20,688
Lily, dear.

225
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:23,774
I know how important Jepoy is to you.

226
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:26,402
But come home first.

227
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:28,821
We need to plan this carefully.

228
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:31,240
<i>I'm begging you.</i>

229
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:33,826
Positive, sir.

230
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:37,746
According to our intel,
that's Camia Cruz's house.

231
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:41,458
Mom…

232
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,255
[whispering] Arnaldo.

233
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:50,342
Stay on the road. Just keep driving.

234
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:53,721
Where is she going?
She went past the house.

235
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:56,056
Mom. Listen to me, Mom.

236
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,559
-Lily…
-<i>I can't go there for now.</i>

237
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:01,145
Don't leave the house,
and don't let anyone know

238
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,563
that I'm the one you're talking to.

239
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:04,314
What are you saying?

240
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:05,691
Is something wrong?

241
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:07,693
<i>Just trust me, Mom.</i>

242
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:11,363
If the Ardientes want to play,
then we'll play.

243
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,906
Let's see who wins.

244
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:18,954
[ominous music playing]

245
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,415
Faster, please.

246
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:22,875
Faster!

247
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:28,714
This means she's not connected
to Camia Cruz.

248
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:31,633
Let's go back.

249
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,719
What about Ma'am Emilia's orders?

250
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:35,429
[phone ringing]

251
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,473
[phone ringing]

252
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,642
-Hello, Ma.
-Hello, Arnaldo, son.

253
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,936
Any news on Ivy Aguas?

254
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:47,399
What's going on?

255
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,109
False alarm.

256
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,652
<i>There's nothing unusual…</i>

257
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:52,696
with Ivy, so I'm going home.

258
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,406
-No, you can't!
<i>-What?</i>

259
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:56,408
I can't follow Ivy the whole day.

260
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:57,451
I have work to do.

261
00:17:57,534 --> 00:18:02,414
You will not come home
until you get information on Ivy

262
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:04,041
<i>Aguas, understood?</i>

263
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,919
Those are your grandfather's orders!

264
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:22,017
-Where are they?
-We lost them.

265
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,644
Maybe they took a shortcut, Sir.

266
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:26,105
Should we go back, Mayor?

267
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:28,565
No.

268
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,361
Let's find that car and follow them.

269
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:37,699
[dramatic music playing]

270
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:39,910
Diego.

271
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:41,495
I should've gone with her.

272
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:44,081
Diego, my daughter is a strong woman.

273
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:45,791
She's brave.

274
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:48,293
Ever since she was young.

275
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:51,672
And we know this more than anyone else.

276
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,132
We just need to…

277
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:56,760
trust that she can handle
whatever's thrown at her.

278
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,809
[tense piano music playing]

279
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:09,064
Be thankful that Ivy Aguas
didn't shoot you in the head.

280
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:10,649
But…

281
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,192
I'm not like Ivy.

282
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:16,029
Because I won't hesitate
to blow your brains out

283
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:18,031
if you don't tell me the truth.

284
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:21,702
Before that, let's play a game.

285
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,081
Hmm…

286
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,333
Do you want to play with this?

287
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,418
This?

288
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:31,587
Hmm…

289
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,422
Boring.

290
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:38,677
I think I prefer this.

291
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,139
Hmm?

292
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:44,766
Do you see this?

293
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:46,560
Hmm?

294
00:19:47,477 --> 00:19:48,437
Ha!

295
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,147
[laughing]

296
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:55,694
Let's try it.
This might convince you to talk.

297
00:19:57,654 --> 00:20:01,783
-[screaming]
-[evil laugh]

298
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:02,784
-Mayor…
-Where's Ivy?

299
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,244
-What is it? Mayor, wait--
-Ivy!

300
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:06,914
-Ouch. Mayor, wait! Mayor!
-Ivy! Don't touch me.

301
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,624
Mayor, you can't just barge
into our house like this.

302
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:11,335
-Search the whole house!
-Mayor, wait!

303
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:13,337
Search every corner in all the rooms.

304
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:15,797
You can't do that. Mayor!

305
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:19,718
-Mayor, you can't do this.
-Yes?

306
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:22,804
[Carlotta] Ivy.

307
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:24,932
Are you looking for me, Mr. Mayor?

308
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:29,561
-Ivy, I thought--
-You thought what?

309
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:35,317
You thought I wasn't here,
so you'd go through my house?

310
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:36,944
Where's your warrant?

311
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:39,071
[tense music playing]

312
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,949
I may be stubborn, Mr. Mayor…

313
00:20:42,574 --> 00:20:46,745
because I won't kill someone
just to prove my loyalty.

314
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:50,499
But that doesn't mean that you
can treat me like a criminal.

315
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,877
Of all people, you?

316
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:57,422
And here I thought…

317
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,092
we were friends.

318
00:21:05,555 --> 00:21:06,431
I'm sorry.

319
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:08,225
Sorry?

320
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:10,727
It's too late for that.

321
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:13,438
You've already hurt me.

322
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:17,776
I think it's for the best
if you leave my house…

323
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:21,947
before I sue you for trespassing.

324
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:27,494
You. Leave my house.

325
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,497
And you, Mr. Mayor, out.

326
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:41,842
[sighs]

327
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:44,303
Ivy.

328
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:50,350
-Do you have a smoke?
-No. Sorry, bro.

329
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,978
They haven't paid us yet.

330
00:21:53,061 --> 00:21:55,981
You're out of funds too?
When's our next pay going to be?

331
00:21:56,231 --> 00:21:57,274
I don't know.

332
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:00,193
-You must stop squandering.
-[Jepoy] Water.

333
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:02,738
-Water.
-He wants water.

334
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:04,740
-Give him water.
-Water, huh?

335
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:19,129
[grunting]

336
00:22:19,212 --> 00:22:20,672
[tense music playing]

337
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:21,923
You want to fight?

338
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,008
[grunts]

339
00:22:25,677 --> 00:22:26,678
He wants to fight.

340
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,182
All right.

341
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:33,143
[tense music playing]

342
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,736
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, thank you.</i>

343
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:47,449
<i>Ever since you rescued me</i>
<i>from that perverted driver…</i>

344
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:51,036
<i>you've always been there for me.</i>

345
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:52,370
<i>You never left me.</i>

346
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:56,458
[somber music playing]

347
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:04,091
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

348
00:23:14,142 --> 00:23:15,102
<i>It is my fault.</i>

349
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,728
<i>You don't know how much</i>
<i>I worried about you.</i>

350
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:19,231
<i>For sure, Emilia's suspecting you now.</i>

351
00:23:19,314 --> 00:23:20,482
<i>I need to do something.</i>

352
00:23:20,565 --> 00:23:24,111
<i>Just make sure you won't</i>
<i>get yourself in danger, Jepoy.</i>

353
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:27,280
<i>-You've done so much for me.</i>
<i>-Ivy, you don't understand.</i>

354
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:28,824
<i>That's not enough because I love you.</i>

355
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:34,496
[Jepoy] <i>There's nothing</i>
<i>I wouldn't do for you, Ivy.</i>

356
00:23:37,749 --> 00:23:41,753
[somber music playing]

357
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:49,010
<i>You have to get out of here, Jepoy.</i>

358
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:52,764
<i>Remember everything you learned</i>
<i>from Miss Prianka.</i>

359
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:55,267
<i>Ivy needs you.</i>

360
00:23:56,768 --> 00:23:58,728
<i>Ivy needs you. Ivy needs you right now.</i>

361
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:10,907
<i>I need to endure this for Ivy.</i>

362
00:24:19,082 --> 00:24:20,458
Mom, what are you doing here?

363
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:24,171
I already told you
that you can't come here.

364
00:24:24,462 --> 00:24:26,256
Lily, I won't feel at ease

365
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:29,176
until I make sure that you're safe.

366
00:24:29,384 --> 00:24:30,844
Mom, I'm fine.

367
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:32,762
Just like I said earlier…

368
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:34,890
I'll do everything I can…

369
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,392
to save Jepoy.

370
00:24:37,475 --> 00:24:39,186
How will you do that?

371
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,645
Mom, trust me.

372
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:44,566
What's important is I know
where they're hiding Jepoy.

373
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:46,526
Lily…

374
00:24:47,444 --> 00:24:50,405
I know that you're strong and brave,

375
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:54,159
but I'm sure that place
will be heavily guarded.

376
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:56,036
I'm worried about you.

377
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:59,497
[tense music playing]

378
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:01,875
Mom, thank you.

379
00:25:03,001 --> 00:25:05,545
But I'm sorry because
I've made up my mind.

380
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:09,257
I'll save my friend. I'll save Jepoy.

381
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:11,259
But you're right.

382
00:25:12,135 --> 00:25:15,555
I need to figure out a way

383
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:19,976
to get back to that place
without the Ardientes' knowing.

384
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:23,730
[tense music playing]

385
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,328
Ma'am.

386
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:42,207
Nanny, please take this away.
I already lost my appetite.

387
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,126
Funny, Emilia.

388
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,045
Between us,

389
00:25:47,128 --> 00:25:50,131
don't you think I'm the one
who should lose my appetite?

390
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:54,427
First of all, you tried
to force me to kill someone.

391
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:57,222
Second, you had your son follow me.

392
00:25:57,973 --> 00:26:00,308
Ivy, I have to protect our bases.

393
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:01,685
It's that simple.

394
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:03,436
I'm sorry if I offended you.

395
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,146
[tense music playing]

396
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:07,190
A little friendly advice, Emilia.

397
00:26:07,357 --> 00:26:10,360
Can you please stop being so paranoid?

398
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:14,572
Why don't you just show
the people of Ardiente

399
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:16,574
that you aren't that easily rattled?

400
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:20,453
I get what you're trying to say, but how?

401
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:23,290
Hold a celebration.

402
00:26:24,374 --> 00:26:25,375
Something that…

403
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:29,504
can bring you closer
to the people of Ardiente.

404
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:33,883
Well, if you don't have
the budget, I can always donate.

405
00:26:34,342 --> 00:26:36,970
-Is this a peace offering?
-Yeah.

406
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:40,140
So shall we start on the wine?

407
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:42,267
Sure.

408
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:45,103
Nanny, corkscrew please! Faster!

409
00:26:46,229 --> 00:26:47,188
[police officer] <i>What did you say?</i>

410
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:49,441
The Ardientes are holding
their bodyguard hostage?

411
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:50,567
Under what grounds?

412
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:53,737
The Ardientes think
that Madrigal is a traitor.

413
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:56,072
That's a personal matter
between the Ardientes

414
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:56,990
and their bodyguard.

415
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:58,033
It will be difficult

416
00:26:58,116 --> 00:26:59,826
to get involved
in that kind of case, Diego.

417
00:26:59,909 --> 00:27:01,369
You should know. You're an Ardiente.

418
00:27:03,788 --> 00:27:05,248
I'm not an Ardiente.

419
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:08,376
[action music playing]

420
00:27:09,085 --> 00:27:11,379
Okay. I'll put it on record.

421
00:27:13,548 --> 00:27:15,383
-Thank you.
-Okay.

422
00:27:19,763 --> 00:27:20,930
[phone ringing]

423
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:23,933
Hello, Grandpa?

424
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:28,021
[Julio] <i>Since I can't rely on</i>
<i>you when it comes to Miss Aguas,</i>

425
00:27:28,104 --> 00:27:33,526
<i>I want you to do something else</i>
<i>to get rid of everyone I doubt.</i>

426
00:27:34,569 --> 00:27:35,570
Okay, Grandpa.

427
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:38,740
I'll take care of Camia Cruz.
You can count on me.

428
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:42,452
[action music playing]

429
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:53,004
[action music continues playing]

430
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:55,757
Miss Camia.

431
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:58,802
Are you expecting company?

432
00:28:00,303 --> 00:28:01,304
No, why?

433
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:06,142
-[car roaring]
-[crickets chirping]

434
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:09,646
[tense music playing]

435
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:21,199
Sir, they've got bodyguards.

436
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:22,909
So what?

437
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:24,577
There are more of us.

438
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:26,621
Are you scared?

439
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:32,794
We'll just do a quick spot-check, ma'am.

440
00:28:32,877 --> 00:28:34,129
Please stay here.

441
00:28:38,258 --> 00:28:40,218
Please check the entire house. Move.

442
00:28:40,427 --> 00:28:43,346
[tense music playing]

443
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:52,105
[suspenseful music playing]

444
00:29:04,701 --> 00:29:05,994
Go on. Break into the house.

445
00:29:10,665 --> 00:29:13,168
[car alarm blaring]

446
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:14,252
Miss Camia, please go inside.

447
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:15,587
-What's going on?
-Get in.

448
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:21,050
-[car horn honking]
-[car alarm blaring]

449
00:29:22,802 --> 00:29:25,764
-[car horn honking]
-[car alarm blaring]

450
00:29:31,853 --> 00:29:33,438
-[alarm stops]
-[car horn honking]

451
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:35,899
[car horn honking]

452
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:42,739
I want you all to be more alert
and careful. Do you understand?

453
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:46,659
Espiritu, did you hear what I said?

454
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:48,411
-Yes, ma'am.
-Talk to your men.

455
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:51,623
Do it now.

456
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:54,959
Lily, you're the one
who needs to be careful.

457
00:29:55,668 --> 00:29:57,754
Since you're always with the Ardientes.

458
00:29:58,338 --> 00:29:59,339
Mom…

459
00:30:00,548 --> 00:30:02,175
Ivy, what you're doing
is really dangerous.

460
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:04,052
Don't put your life at risk just for this.

461
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:09,349
Diego, you don't understand.

462
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:12,894
I need to save Jepoy.

463
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:15,230
What if you get caught?

464
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:17,941
Ivy, they'll hurt you.

465
00:30:18,650 --> 00:30:21,110
I will never forgive myself
if something bad happens to you.

466
00:30:21,194 --> 00:30:24,948
And I won't forgive myself
if I let them kill Jepoy.

467
00:30:25,031 --> 00:30:28,076
[somber music playing]

468
00:30:28,451 --> 00:30:29,744
He's my family.

469
00:30:32,247 --> 00:30:33,790
He's my friend, like my brother.

470
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:38,086
Wouldn't you do the same
for your loved ones?

471
00:30:43,216 --> 00:30:47,470
I need to help Jepoy. I will save Jepoy.

472
00:30:48,972 --> 00:30:51,057
Ivy, I know I can't stop you.

473
00:30:53,393 --> 00:30:54,978
But let me protect you at least.

474
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:58,022
I will help you.

475
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:02,277
Thank you, Diego.

476
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:13,580
[tense music playing]

477
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,373
-Ivy, I'll come with you.
-No, Diego.

478
00:31:16,624 --> 00:31:17,625
Stay here.

479
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:22,171
We'll push through with the plan
until I get Jepoy out.

480
00:31:23,131 --> 00:31:25,091
-But, Ivy…
-Diego!

481
00:31:25,884 --> 00:31:27,594
How many times do I have to tell you?

482
00:31:28,761 --> 00:31:30,096
I can protect myself.

483
00:31:30,179 --> 00:31:32,390
It's more dangerous
if both of us head on inside.

484
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:34,392
We might get caught.

485
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:38,980
If they catch me,
I'll try my best to escape.

486
00:31:40,523 --> 00:31:42,233
Diego, please understand.

487
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:46,070
Ivy, be careful.

488
00:31:55,288 --> 00:31:58,750
[action music playing]

489
00:32:12,096 --> 00:32:13,097
Jepoy.

490
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:16,351
Where did they take you?

491
00:32:26,569 --> 00:32:28,821
-This is for you, my friend.
-[woman] Thank you.

492
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:30,949
You're welcome. Use it well, okay?

493
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:33,576
[Julio] I hope that can help you.

494
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:35,161
[Claire] Oh. Here. Here she is.

495
00:32:35,244 --> 00:32:38,831
[Julio] Okay. Come back
if you need anything else.

496
00:32:39,123 --> 00:32:40,458
[Emilia] Use all those medicines.

497
00:32:40,541 --> 00:32:42,752
[Julio] If you need anything
else, don't hesitate to ask.

498
00:32:42,835 --> 00:32:45,088
We're here if you need anything else.

499
00:32:45,171 --> 00:32:47,632
-[Emilia] Sir, you flatter me.
-[Julio] You're welcome, ma'am.

500
00:32:47,715 --> 00:32:49,884
Come back if you need anything else.

501
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:51,219
-Sir.
-Thank you.

502
00:32:51,552 --> 00:32:54,514
Thank you, Congressman and Mrs. Emilia.

503
00:32:55,014 --> 00:32:57,850
We don't believe
the accusations against you.

504
00:32:58,101 --> 00:33:00,853
For us, the Ardientes are innocent.

505
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:03,314
-Thank you.
-After all you've done

506
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:07,026
to help us, it's fair how
you're dealing with criminals.

507
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,569
Thank you, ma'am.

508
00:33:09,195 --> 00:33:13,199
Truth be told, we're very
grateful to you for trusting us.

509
00:33:13,408 --> 00:33:18,496
You're the reason we keep
doing what we do.

510
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:19,956
Thank you.

511
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:22,250
Thank you, everyone. Rest assured that--

512
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:26,087
Emilia. Since you're a true Ardiente…

513
00:33:26,629 --> 00:33:28,214
I believe it's only right

514
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:31,592
for you to accommodate our townspeople.

515
00:33:32,635 --> 00:33:35,179
-Thank you, Papa.
-By all means, please.

516
00:33:35,763 --> 00:33:37,056
[action music playing]

517
00:33:37,140 --> 00:33:38,391
Ivy, are you okay?

518
00:33:38,474 --> 00:33:39,600
What happened?

519
00:33:39,767 --> 00:33:42,478
Jepoy isn't there. Jepoy's gone!

520
00:33:42,562 --> 00:33:44,689
I don't know where the Ardientes took him!

521
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:49,485
Don't worry. We'll find him for sure.

522
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:51,904
I'll find him, Diego.

523
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:54,407
[ominous music playing]

524
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:56,409
I need to go to the Ardientes now.

525
00:33:57,535 --> 00:33:58,536
Let's go.

526
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:03,583
Please come back. If you
need anything, come to us.

527
00:34:03,666 --> 00:34:06,210
-All right.
-Oh, there's Ivy! Wait, Papa.

528
00:34:06,335 --> 00:34:08,671
-Okay.
-Ivy, you're finally here.

529
00:34:08,755 --> 00:34:09,756
Emilia.

530
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:13,593
You know, your idea is just so brilliant.

531
00:34:13,676 --> 00:34:15,053
It's like we're making a statement

532
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:16,929
to our political rivals.

533
00:34:17,346 --> 00:34:19,223
I'm glad you see it that way.

534
00:34:19,348 --> 00:34:24,479
Maybe by now, Congressman,
you won't doubt me anymore.

535
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:29,400
Miss Aguas, never again.

536
00:34:32,153 --> 00:34:34,864
All right, I'll just stay over
there so I won't bother you.

537
00:34:35,198 --> 00:34:37,116
-Excuse me.
-Thank you again.

538
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:41,287
[tense music playing]

539
00:34:42,997 --> 00:34:45,208
-[Emilia clears throat]
-[Julio] Did you invite her?

540
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:47,835
[Emilia] Yes, Papa. This was her idea.

541
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:49,587
Oh, I see.

542
00:34:49,670 --> 00:34:51,339
The governor must be crying.

543
00:34:54,258 --> 00:34:57,512
I don't know why they asked us
to transfer him.

544
00:34:58,012 --> 00:34:59,430
Why don't you just admit it?!

545
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:02,517
Do you think anyone will come to save you?

546
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:03,601
[Jepoy grunts]

547
00:35:03,893 --> 00:35:05,645
-Stay here.
-[Jepoy grunts]

548
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:10,483
[ominous music playing]

549
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:13,361
[phone ringing]

550
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:15,404
-Hello?
-[Arnaldo] <i>Hello.</i>

551
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:16,614
Have you moved him yet?

552
00:35:18,741 --> 00:35:20,076
Yes, Mayor. We already did.

553
00:35:20,576 --> 00:35:21,577
Okay, good.

554
00:35:26,457 --> 00:35:29,043
Grandpa, Madrigal was
transferred to another hideout,

555
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:30,253
just as Mom ordered.

556
00:35:32,171 --> 00:35:34,549
That's good to hear. Since more and more

557
00:35:34,632 --> 00:35:37,802
of our enemies are popping up,
that was a good move.

558
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,763
You see, Emilia.

559
00:35:42,181 --> 00:35:43,766
After all these years…

560
00:35:44,934 --> 00:35:47,228
you eventually learned something from me.

561
00:35:47,937 --> 00:35:49,480
[Emilia] Get your grandfather a chair.

562
00:35:49,897 --> 00:35:51,107
Papa, I'll just stay there.

563
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:52,191
Okay, Emilia.

564
00:35:53,109 --> 00:35:54,443
[Arnaldo] Grandpa, have a seat.

565
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:57,280
-Thank you, Arnaldo.
-I'll mingle with the people.

566
00:35:57,363 --> 00:35:58,364
[Julio] Go ahead.

567
00:36:04,453 --> 00:36:06,372
<i>What did you do to Jepoy?</i>

568
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:08,249
<i>Is he still alive?</i>

569
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:11,294
Where did you move him?
Where did you take him?

570
00:36:11,419 --> 00:36:15,506
[action music playing]

571
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:28,102
Dad…

572
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:33,149
Dad, I saw your car outside
Miss Camia's house last night.

573
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:34,817
What were you doing there?

574
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:38,529
I heard the Ardientes
wanted to hurt Camia.

575
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:41,115
So I did something to trigger a search.

576
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:44,744
But you know the situation
you're in, right?

577
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:46,662
Miss Camia doesn't want to see you.

578
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:49,749
I know. But I can't sit back
and do nothing.

579
00:36:50,082 --> 00:36:51,959
I'm doing everything I can to protect her.

580
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:55,129
[dramatic piano music playing]

581
00:36:55,755 --> 00:36:57,340
I know you understand me, son.

582
00:37:00,009 --> 00:37:01,010
Dad.

583
00:37:01,594 --> 00:37:02,762
Dad, where are you going?

584
00:37:07,516 --> 00:37:09,810
We've got plenty of medicines over there.

585
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:12,230
Just tell them what you need, okay?

586
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:14,023
-Thank you, Mayor.
-All right.

587
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:16,567
[Arnaldo] Get yours too.
Just tell us what you need.

588
00:37:24,325 --> 00:37:25,910
[clears throat] Miss Aguas.

589
00:37:27,745 --> 00:37:30,414
Uh, you seem quieter than usual.
Are you all right?

590
00:37:31,123 --> 00:37:32,375
Tell me. I'll do what I can.

591
00:37:34,377 --> 00:37:37,672
Mr. Mayor, to be honest,
I really want to talk to you.

592
00:37:40,007 --> 00:37:42,510
Have you already forgotten what you did?

593
00:37:45,012 --> 00:37:46,806
Yes, about that…

594
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,684
Not here.

595
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:53,729
Let's talk somewhere else.

596
00:37:56,732 --> 00:37:59,151
Let's go somewhere private.

597
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:02,071
I want you to myself.

598
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:06,200
If you don't mind.

599
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:08,995
[ominous music playing]

600
00:38:15,751 --> 00:38:17,169
[goon] <i>I feel sorry for Madrigal.</i>

601
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:19,213
He looks horrible. He can't even stand.

602
00:38:19,463 --> 00:38:20,464
Forget about him.

603
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:22,258
Let's go, I'm starving!
Let's take a break.

604
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:23,301
Sure.

605
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:27,388
[ominous music playing]

606
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:39,400
[groans]

607
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:42,194
[grunting]

608
00:38:55,875 --> 00:38:58,210
[breathing heavily]

609
00:39:28,240 --> 00:39:32,244
[somber music playing]

610
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:39,502
Miss Aguas.

611
00:39:42,088 --> 00:39:43,089
Mr. Mayor.

612
00:39:45,007 --> 00:39:47,468
I think I owe you an apology.

613
00:39:48,928 --> 00:39:51,347
I'm sorry for barging
into your house like that?

614
00:39:51,472 --> 00:39:53,307
[sleazy music playing]

615
00:39:57,978 --> 00:39:59,313
Let's not talk about it.

616
00:40:02,233 --> 00:40:03,401
Okay, then.

617
00:40:05,319 --> 00:40:06,695
What is it you want to talk about?

618
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:20,334
What's this?

619
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:26,382
What else? It's a security camera.

620
00:40:26,924 --> 00:40:30,553
And I don't know
why I found one in my mansion.

621
00:40:31,387 --> 00:40:35,224
But I think I know who put it there.

622
00:40:38,018 --> 00:40:41,021
-Madrigal…
-Exactly! It's Madrigal!

623
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:44,024
I don't know why he put that
in my mansion. Why?

624
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:46,569
Just because I'm affiliated
with the Ardientes,

625
00:40:46,652 --> 00:40:48,237
he'll go after me too?

626
00:40:48,612 --> 00:40:50,948
[tense music playing]

627
00:40:51,198 --> 00:40:52,575
Ivy, I'm sorry.

628
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:55,035
That man needs to be dealt with.

629
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:58,747
Yes, he needs to be punished.
I want to see him.

630
00:41:04,378 --> 00:41:05,421
I'm so full.

631
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,009
What the? Where's Madrigal?

632
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:12,344
We're in big trouble.

633
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:14,346
Let's find him!

634
00:41:15,681 --> 00:41:19,268
[action music playing]

635
00:41:32,531 --> 00:41:35,534
To reciprocate the love

636
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:38,913
and trust you've shown the Ardientes,

637
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:43,209
starting today,
I'll be giving away rations

638
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:47,171
and allowances to all of you every day.

639
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:50,174
-[applauding]
-[cheering]

640
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:55,638
Wait, I know you're pleased
with what I said,

641
00:41:55,721 --> 00:41:57,806
but I'm sorry I made a little mistake.

642
00:41:58,015 --> 00:42:00,059
I'm sorry about that. I'm still human.

643
00:42:00,142 --> 00:42:02,436
Maybe not every day
because I'll go bankrupt.

644
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:07,942
Every month, I promise
you'll receive rations

645
00:42:08,025 --> 00:42:10,778
and allowances from us.

646
00:42:11,779 --> 00:42:15,824
That is testimony
to the Ardientes' love for you,

647
00:42:16,283 --> 00:42:18,994
especially mine,

648
00:42:19,745 --> 00:42:25,125
for your kindness
and obedience as my children.

649
00:42:25,584 --> 00:42:32,049
And now, to ask how everyone
in this town is doing,

650
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:35,803
I'd like to present to you, our trusted…

651
00:42:36,387 --> 00:42:39,848
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

652
00:42:39,932 --> 00:42:43,727
-[cheering]
-[applauding]

653
00:42:44,979 --> 00:42:46,480
[tense music playing]

654
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,399
Thank you very much, Papa.

655
00:42:48,691 --> 00:42:52,486
A round of applause
for our Señor Julio Ardiente.

656
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:53,862
-[cheering]
-[applauding]

657
00:42:53,946 --> 00:42:56,031
A father to us all!

658
00:42:57,199 --> 00:43:01,412
And yes, it's true that
my father has appointed me to--

659
00:43:01,495 --> 00:43:04,582
[phone ringing]

660
00:43:04,665 --> 00:43:08,586
Like I said, to serve you as--

661
00:43:10,337 --> 00:43:11,672
[goon] <i>Madrigal got away.</i>

662
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:16,218
This can't be. Hold this.

663
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:17,928
-[Julio] Emilia!
-Emilia!

664
00:43:22,891 --> 00:43:23,892
Emilia!

665
00:43:27,354 --> 00:43:30,065
[action music playing]

666
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:33,527
[grunting, panting]

667
00:43:36,614 --> 00:43:38,407
Madrigal! Stop!

668
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:41,410
[Jepoy grunts]

669
00:43:43,162 --> 00:43:44,288
[unintelligible]

670
00:43:45,497 --> 00:43:46,707
Get up! Get up!

671
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:47,958
[grunting]

672
00:43:48,042 --> 00:43:49,001
Come here!

673
00:43:49,084 --> 00:43:49,918
[grunting]

674
00:43:54,506 --> 00:43:55,507
[screaming]

675
00:43:56,175 --> 00:43:57,176
[screaming]

676
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:00,596
[screaming]

677
00:44:05,851 --> 00:44:07,728
You know why I wanna him?

678
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:13,817
I wanna see him because I regret
not taking Madrigal's life

679
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:15,986
when Emilia gave me the chance!

680
00:44:16,737 --> 00:44:18,781
He has some nerve doing this to me!

681
00:44:18,864 --> 00:44:22,201
[somber music playing]

682
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:28,040
I understand.

683
00:44:34,505 --> 00:44:35,714
You can still do it.

684
00:44:38,258 --> 00:44:40,511
But Madrigal isn't
in his old detention room.

685
00:44:40,594 --> 00:44:41,720
My mother had him moved.

686
00:44:47,142 --> 00:44:48,102
You moved him?

687
00:44:50,687 --> 00:44:51,688
Really?

688
00:44:54,358 --> 00:44:55,359
Where?

689
00:44:56,318 --> 00:44:59,780
They probably moved him
somewhere your mother

690
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,990
and grandfather can torture him even more.

691
00:45:03,575 --> 00:45:07,121
I want to see Madrigal
being tortured with my own eyes

692
00:45:07,329 --> 00:45:08,288
because he deserves it.

693
00:45:08,372 --> 00:45:12,376
[tense music swelling]

694
00:45:15,629 --> 00:45:16,630
Maybe…

695
00:45:17,798 --> 00:45:19,383
It's time I took you to him.

696
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:24,888
[tense music playing]

697
00:45:26,306 --> 00:45:27,391
I owe you one.

698
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:31,437
[tense music continues playing]

699
00:45:50,372 --> 00:45:53,375
[somber piano music playing]

700
00:46:21,987 --> 00:46:23,530
Raul dropped by again tonight.

701
00:46:24,531 --> 00:46:26,158
[sighs] Good thing
he didn't cause trouble.

702
00:46:26,241 --> 00:46:29,620
[somber piano music playing]

703
00:46:40,756 --> 00:46:44,676
If you thought you could escape
without us knowing,

704
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:47,221
well, you were wrong! Idiot!

705
00:46:53,018 --> 00:46:55,646
Let's see what else we can do with you.

706
00:46:56,897 --> 00:46:57,898
Hmm…

707
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:00,526
How about this?

708
00:47:00,817 --> 00:47:02,152
[drill whirring]

709
00:47:02,236 --> 00:47:03,237
Hmm?

710
00:47:04,404 --> 00:47:05,405
[chuckles]

711
00:47:06,281 --> 00:47:07,616
Who do you work for?

712
00:47:08,700 --> 00:47:09,743
Answer me!

713
00:47:10,452 --> 00:47:11,954
Who's your boss?!

714
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:15,582
[drill whirring]

715
00:47:16,083 --> 00:47:17,209
Emilia.

716
00:47:18,544 --> 00:47:19,962
Stop playing games.

717
00:47:20,921 --> 00:47:24,424
Torture him and get the answer we need.

718
00:47:26,134 --> 00:47:27,177
Okay, Papa.

719
00:47:28,512 --> 00:47:31,098
Hang him upside down! Now!

720
00:47:31,181 --> 00:47:34,184
[suspenseful music playing]

721
00:47:39,064 --> 00:47:42,693
Madrigal, I am not in the mood for games.

722
00:47:42,776 --> 00:47:44,027
Do I have the time?

723
00:47:45,404 --> 00:47:48,031
Now, this is going to be easy.

724
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:51,618
You will tell me who your boss is.

725
00:47:52,369 --> 00:47:53,370
If you don't,

726
00:47:54,413 --> 00:47:59,876
I'll drill this into your forehead
until your brains spill out,

727
00:47:59,960 --> 00:48:03,380
and that will be
the death of you. Is that clear?

728
00:48:03,463 --> 00:48:07,634
[suspenseful music playing]

729
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:13,515
[drill whirring]

730
00:48:17,561 --> 00:48:18,812
[phone rings]

731
00:48:18,895 --> 00:48:19,896
Hello, Mama?

732
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:21,815
Any news on Madrigal?

733
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:23,984
Who's his boss? Who does he work for?

734
00:48:24,943 --> 00:48:28,488
[suspenseful music playing]

735
00:49:07,736 --> 00:49:09,946
[Natalie] <i>Everyone comes back</i>
<i>for a reason.</i>

736
00:49:10,447 --> 00:49:13,116
<i>I still think about how my dad died.</i>

737
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:18,246
<i>I know someone had him killed,</i>
<i>and I wanna know who it is.</i>

738
00:49:19,873 --> 00:49:22,209
[Julio] <i>You are of no use now, Madrigal.</i>

739
00:49:22,292 --> 00:49:24,002
<i>Goodbye. Go ahead. Do it!</i>

740
00:49:26,755 --> 00:49:30,676
<i>As long as I'm in power, no traitor</i>

741
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:33,929
<i>or rebel can ever bring</i>
<i>the Ardientes down!</i>

742
00:49:34,012 --> 00:49:35,514
[Diego] <i>I'll run for governor.</i>

743
00:49:35,597 --> 00:49:39,351
<i>I will do everything</i>
<i>in my power to help you win.</i>

744
00:49:39,434 --> 00:49:42,979
[theme music playing]
